{
  "dom_id": "step-q269771",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"70px\" align=\"center\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n\n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$38$</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\">$34$</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}-{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}-{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2{y}_{1} & 2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot 2+1 \\\\ 3+2\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 14 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{3}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & {x}_{1} & 1 \\\\ 1 & {x}_{3} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 14 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 38 & 52 & 34\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
